 <!-- <h2>Parametric Drawing via $Drawing</h2>
<p>A .cdrw sidecar drawing joins the worksheet calculation cycle: worksheet variables feed the drawing declared inputs, and every recalculation redraws the geometry with computed dimensions. </p>
<p>Edit the values below and the drawing follows. -->
 <h3>Truss with computed dimensions</h3>
 <svg class="drawing" data-drawing-src="Truss Drawing/truss-example.cdrw" style="width:100%;" version="1.1" viewbox="-80 -120 166 243" width="100%" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <style type="text/css">
   .drawing text { fill:#3c4852; font-family:'Segoe UI', Sans; paint-order: stroke; stroke:#fdfdfc; stroke-width:4; stroke-linejoin:round; }
.drawing .cdrw-geom line { stroke-linecap: round; }
.drawing .cdrw-dims line { stroke:#7b8790; stroke-width:1.5; fill:none; }
.drawing .cdrw-dims text { fill:#7b8790; }
.drawing .cdrw-callouts text { fill:#56616b; }
.drawing text.cdrw-title { font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight:600; fill:#4a5560; }
  </style>
  <text class="cdrw-title" font-size="34" x="-60" y="-70">Truss Members</text>
  <text class="cdrw-title" font-size="18" x="-60" y="-40">Gravity load</text>
